==History==
2017
*The Mega Knight was once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Mega Knight Challenge]], which started on 25/8/2017. In this [[Tournament|challenge]], the player would build a [[Battle Decks|deck]] which included the Mega Knight. If the player achieved 12 wins, they obtained the Mega Knight early,
*From 31/8/2017 through 4/9/2017, the [[Shop]] had a special offer where [[Arenas|Arena]] 10+ players could buy up to 4 Super Magical [[Chests]] at the normal price that had a 50% chance to contain a Mega Knight with the first Chest and guaranteed with the second. If a Mega Knight was obtained in the first Chest, then the second one would not guarantee it. The process was repeated with the second pair of Chests.
*The Mega Knight [[Cards|card]] was generally released on 8/9/2017.
*On 9/10/2017, the [[Version History#Epic Quests Update (9/10/2017)|Epic Quests Update]], fixed a bug where the Mega Knight would jump even if he was less than 4 tiles away from his target.
2018
*On 12/2/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (12/2/2018)|Balance Update]], decreased both his spawn and jump damage by 25% and decreased his spawn area radius to 2.2 tiles (from 2.5 tiles).
*On 4/6/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/6/2018)|Balance Update]], increased both his spawn and jump damage by 23%, but also decreased his damage by 7.5%.
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], decreased his minimum jump range to 3.5 tiles (from 4 tiles).
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Legendary}} cards start at Level 9 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 5).
*On 5/11/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (5/11/2018)|Balance Update]], decreased the Mega Knight's attack time interval to 1.7 seconds (from 1.8 seconds) and his first attack time interval to 0.5 seconds (from 0.6 seconds).
2019
*On 28/1/2019, the [[Version History#January%202019%20Update%20(28/1/2019)|January 2019 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Mega Knight from Hog Mountain to Royal Arena.
*On 1/7/2019, the [[Version History#July%202019%20Update%20(1/7/2019)|July 2019 Update]], increased the Mega Knight's range to 1.2 tiles (from 1 tile), now classified as Melee: Medium.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], added a card render to the Mega Knight's card info screen.
2021
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
*On 1/11/2021, an [[Version History#Optional%20Update%20(1/11/2021)|Optional Update]], made it so that the Mega Knight cannot be forever stunned by [[Zappies]] or [[Electro Wizard]].
*On 15/11/2021, a [[Version History#Minor%20Update%20(15/11/2021)|Minor Update]], allowed the Mega Knight to deal damage to an [[Archer Queen]] if she's cloaked during his jump.
2022
*On 4/4/2022, the [[Version History#April%202022%20Update%20(4/4/2022)|April 2022 Update]], decreased the Mega Knight's spawn damage by 20%.
*On 27/6/2022, the [[Version History#Summer%202022%20Update%20(27/6/2022)|Summer 2022 Update]], added the Superhero Landing [[Card Mastery]] task for the Mega Knight.
*On 2/8/2022, a [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(2/8/2022)|Balance Update]], decreased the time required for charging his jump to 0.9 seconds (from 1.1 seconds).
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Mega Knight from Royal Arena to Electro Valley.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2024
*On 14/9/2024, the [[Mega Knight/Evolution|Mega Knight’s Evolution]] was added.
2025
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], increased the Mega Knight's spawn damage by 0.23%.

