==Trivia== 
*The word ''"Knight"'' comes from the German "''Knecht"'', meaning servant or vassal. Originally, knights were associated with mounted warriors, later being considered a class of lower nobility, until eventually, knighthood had become associated with the ideals of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chivalry chivalry], a code of conduct for the perfect courtly Christian warrior. Often, a knight was a vassal who served as an elite fighter or a bodyguard for a lord, with payment in the form of land holdings.
**In the Chinese and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Mega Knight's name translates to "Super Knight". In the Italian and Arabic language settings of the game, the Mega Knight's name translates to "Great Knight" and "Giant Knight" respectively.
**The Mega Knight is 1 of 20 [[cards]] associated with nobility, with the others being [[Knight]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Royal Giant]], [[Royal Delivery]], [[Tower Princess]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Prince]], [[Raging Prince]], [[Princess]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Spirit Empress]], [[Super Knight]], [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Royal Chef]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], and the [[Little Prince]].
*The Mega Knight is one of the first [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] cards to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], Knight, [[Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Bats]], Royal Recruits, [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], Royal Hogs, [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], Prince, [[Balloon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], Royal Ghost, [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Mega Knight, the [[Electro Wizard]], and the Ice Wizard are the only troops that deal spawn damage. Unlike the other two, the Mega Knight's spawn damage does not affect air troops.
*The Mega Knight and Lava Hound are the most expensive permanent {{Rarity|Legendary}} cards, costing 7 [[Elixir]].
*The Mega Knight is 1 of 14 troops that has been featured with a [[Buff#Rage|Rage]] [[buff]], the others being [[Electro Spirit]], Giant, Zappies, [[Guards]], Giant Skeleton, Goblin Giant, Electro Dragon, Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], Ram Rider, Electro Wizard, [[Sparky]], and Royal Ghost.
*The Mega Knight, along with the [[Minions]], Bomber, Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Ice Spirit]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Ice Golem]], Dart Goblin, Elixir Golem, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], Guards, Baby Dragon, P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, [[Golem]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, [[Executioner]], [[Inferno Dragon]], Royal Ghost, and Lava Hound, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*Since the description implies it lands with the force of "1,000 mustaches", it is implied that the force of 1 mustache deals approximately 0.429 damage at Tournament Standard.
*The Mega Knight was originally a Knight who had been teased by other Knights for having small and weak hands, as seen in a [https://www.youtube.com/shorts/TfVrkZ0bcks short].
**Previous theories by fans were that the Mega Knight was the [[w:c:clashofclans:Builder|Builder]] from Clash of Clans, but this was [https://www.reddit.com/r/ClashRoyale/comments/6x01fo/clash_royale_ama_qa_collection/ disproven by Supercell]. Although fans continue to speculate and are not entirely convinced.
*When the Mega Knight is defeated, his maces fall to the ground. The other units that drop items upon death are the Knight, Rascal Boy, [[Mega Minion]], Dark Prince, Executioner, Sparky, Fisherman, Super Knight, Golden Knight, and the Little Prince.
*The Mega Knight is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Mega Knight is the subject of 3 [[Emotes]].
**The Mega Knight is the subject of a [[King's Tower|Tower Skin]].
**The Mega Knight is the subject of a [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] item.
***The Mega Knight is one of the first troops to be the subject of a Battle Banner item, along with the [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A,]] Prince, Giant Skeleton, [[Super Witch]], and the Golden Knight.
*A [[Clone|cloned]] Mega Knight does not fall from the sky when deployed.
*On 27/3/2023, a [[Training Camp|Trainer]] was added to the game called Boss Cheddar, and used a Level 18 Mega Knight in their [[Battle Decks|deck]], despite the highest Level being Level 14 at the time. This Trainer was removed on 18/4/2023.
*On 1/4/2024, a Clash Royale [https://youtube.com/shorts/zkmPW505IL8?si=vtvLO_UVVs-tguhS video] on Youtube showcased a fake Mega Knight's [[Card Evolution|Evolution]]. The Evolved Mega Knight had higher spawn damage and spawn radius, infinite jump range, lower time to charge his jump, could target air troops, and required 0 cycles to deploy. However, it never made it into the game.

